From 7a4f0b6cfd517fa90f7c5bc69286e28df68fc4f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:04:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] pin clock in capability-drop ready-episode test

test_claims_before_current_ready_episode_do_not_veto_capability_drop flaked in CI
(run 43730602142 job 132862143858, [shared_blocker_wake]: final assert got None).

Why: the test captured now = int(time.time()) and then let _wake / _append_event stamp
the ready-episode event with a fresh int(time.time()). When a second boundary fell
between the two, ready_since became now+1, so the final claim moved to `now` sat
before the current episode and correctly did not veto. The product contract (a claim
in the same second as the episode start counts, `created_at >= since`) is unchanged;
the test's premise "episode starts at now" was only true without a boundary crossing.
[continued] has the same exposure; [clear_already_ready] starts no new episode.

Fix: pin time.time to `now` before seeding (as the sibling same-second test already
does), so the episode event is stamped exactly at `now`. No product change, no
sleeps or retries; old-episode non-veto and recent-claim veto asserts are unchanged.

Proof:
- RED: unchanged test under a pytest plugin that advances time.time one whole second
  per call during the test body: [continued] and [shared_blocker_wake] fail at the
  final move_refusal assert (AssertionError: assert None), as in CI.
- GREEN: same hostile clock, fixed test: 3 passed.
- Mutant (ready_since floor removed from klb.read) still fails [continued].
- Whole file via hermes-core-wt test: 43 passed; exact parameter 5/5.
---
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_label_backlog_wait.py | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_label_backlog_wait.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_label_backlog_wait.py
index a45ca22c87860dfb0253503f9c96593e1253f9bb..6dfc42d3e736cc9fc9c13ae880f6b7d77b793b04 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_label_backlog_wait.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_label_backlog_wait.py
@@ -267,10 +267,13 @@ def test_hub_update_hold_does_not_hide_recent_pool_claims(hub):
 
 
 @pytest.mark.parametrize("transition", ["continued", "shared_blocker_wake", "clear_already_ready"])
-def test_claims_before_current_ready_episode_do_not_veto_capability_drop(hub, transition):
+def test_claims_before_current_ready_episode_do_not_veto_capability_drop(hub, monkeypatch, transition):
     from hermes_cli import kanban_label_backlog as klb
-    tid = _seed(hub.conn, claims=1)
     now = int(time.time())
+    # The ready-episode event is stamped by the event writer's clock. Pinned, it starts exactly at ``now``, so the
+    # final claim at ``now`` is inside the episode; unpinned, a second boundary before the write excluded it.
+    monkeypatch.setattr(time, "time", lambda: now)
+    tid = _seed(hub.conn, claims=1)
     with kb.write_txn(hub.conn):
         hub.conn.execute("UPDATE task_events SET created_at=? WHERE kind='claimed'", (now - 60,))
         if transition == "shared_blocker_wake":
